- op: create  # a27c
  at: '2026-09-06T20:19:52Z'  # a27c
  by: agent  # a27c
  actor: jgstern_agent  # a27c
  clock: 1  # a27c
  nonce: a27c  # a27c
  data:  # a27c
    kind: work_item  # a27c
    title: "Exit status minted as untrusted_input at os.wait*/Child.wait but not at call/check_call/system/Run/Command::status: one value, two verdicts (INV-lozat's acknowledged disagreement) -- reconcile under the WI-dozul rule after T2's delta"  # a27c
    status: todo_hard  # a27c
    priority: 3  # a27c
    parent:  # a27c
    tags:  # a27c
    - taint  # a27c
    - catalogue  # a27c
    - io_boundary  # a27c
    isbefore: []  # a27c
    duplicate_of: []  # a27c
    not_duplicate_of: []  # a27c
    pr_ref:  # a27c
    description: "FOUND by the 2026-09-06 taint-label concept audit\n(~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/concept-audit-taint-label_09062026.md, Pair 2), and\nalready named in INV-lozat's own thread as \"a disagreement with two shipped\nrows rather than an oversight\" -- acknowledged, never filed.\n\nTHE TWO VERDICTS ON ONE VALUE. An exit status is eight bits the child chose.\n  python.yaml:698-699  os.wait / waitpid / wait3 / wait4 / waitid -> ipc_recv\n      (\"Reaping a child collects its exit status - data received from\n      another process\") -> MINTS untrusted_input.\n  rust.yaml:456-461    std::process::Child.wait / try_wait -> ipc_recv,\n      citing the python row.\n  python.yaml:751-753  subprocess.call / check_call stay launch-only (\"return\n      a returncode\"); INV-lozat: \"eight bits the program chose is not the\n      child's message\" -- likewise os.system, Cmd.Run, Command::status,\n      rawSystem, callProcess. -> mint NOTHING.\n\nTHE RULE THAT DECIDES IT is the one WI-dozul was ruled on today: a value the\nfar side CHOSE from a constrained set is still a transfer under ADR-0049\nruling 1 (accept's peer address; a DNS answer), it mints, and the claims'\nhonesty is kept by the value-shape property (WI-gohok's mechanism, source\nside) and by MEASUREMENT (the 0003 marginal delta, awaits_bakeoff_validation).\nUnder that rule the CONSISTENT fix is the omission side: row call /\ncheck_call / system / Run / Command::status as ipc_recv `simultaneous: true`\nbeside their subprocess row, as check_output already is. Under INV-lozat's\nreading the fix is the removal side: drop the wait rows (ADR-0049 ruling 3:\nrepresented crossing -- the child's BYTES stay represented by check_output /\nwait_with_output / Command::output). This item does not pick; the cost is the\nsame kind WI-dozul's is (a source at every subprocess.call in the corpus; 54\nsubprocess.run in beads alone), so it is SEQUENCED BEHIND WI-dozul (T2 of the\narc tail) and decided on T2's delta: if forward-lookup flows read majority\nnot-useful there, this family goes the removal way; otherwise the omission\nway, measured the same way. Either way: parity across python / rust / go /\nhaskell / elixir; every moved row read back; never pin a removal.\n\nPositive control for closure: one `subprocess.call(cmd)` fixture and one\n`os.waitpid` fixture through the production CLI, cold cache, asserting the\nSAME verdict for the same value on both."  # a27c
    fields: {}  # a27c
- op: discuss  # 9ae2
  at: '2026-10-03T15:41:59Z'  # 9ae2
  by: agent  # 9ae2
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 9ae2
  clock: 2  # 9ae2
  nonce: 9ae2  # 9ae2
  message: "WORK DONE 2026-10-03 (concurrent run, stage 2). Branch jgstern-agent/fix/lanos (local, not pushed), worktree ~/hg_wt/lanos, from origin/dev e8d9e89ca4. Commits: b3ac13e0a9 (rows + caveat registry + tests), de6aacfe6c (WI-rivur row 3 note, see that item), 21d86e2280 (subprocess.run withdrawn from the choice-shaped disclosure). Report: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/decontend/run_10032026/lanos.md.\n\nT2 = WI-dozul (WI-nazos arc tail entry 2026-09-06). LANDED: PR #839, 26578f5d7e, an ancestor of the branch point. Its delta (measurement 0019) is 6 added / 0 correct, and 0019 itself records that the trigger's CONDITION fired but its premise did not, that its cohort \"cannot answer the trigger's question\", and that nothing in it argues for removing rows. This item's removal branch was keyed to that same trigger, so the record leaves the WI-dozul ruling standing and the item goes the OMISSION way. Not blocked.\n\nDECIDED: omission. ipc_recv rows (simultaneous with the launch row where the call launches): python subprocess.call, subprocess.run (status only; its stdout half stays unclaimed), os.system, subprocess.Popen.wait/poll; rust std::process::Command.status; go os/exec.Cmd.Run, os/exec.Cmd.Wait (new), os.Process.Wait (new); haskell System.Process.system/rawSystem/waitForProcess, getProcessExitCode (new). NOT rowed, each read against its API: check_call (returns 0; the status rides the exception), Cmd.Start, Command::spawn, createProcess, callProcess/callCommand. elixir: no member (System.cmd/shell already mint). The choice_shaped_source caveat (WI-jivih) now covers the members via CHOICE_SHAPED_QUALIFIED_SOURCES ((module, name), because bare call/system/Run would have caveated platform.system), EXCEPT subprocess.run (see the measurement). Python `system` joined ambiguous_names (a hint-less bare system() had flipped from platform.system to os.system by row order alone).\n\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE, production CLI, fresh cache per run, claim untrusted-input-no-subprocess, one repo per call shape, BEFORE = e8d9e89ca4 tree, AFTER = branch tip:\n  py os.waitpid / os.wait       violated -> violated (ipc_recv)\n  py subprocess.call / os.system / subprocess.run / Popen.poll / Popen.wait(sink check_call)   confirmed_with_caveats -> violated (ipc_recv)\n  py check_call (control)       confirmed_with_caveats -> confirmed_with_caveats\n  rs Child.wait                 violated -> violated;  rs Command.status   confirmed_with_caveats -> violated\n  go Cmd.Run                    confirmed_with_caveats -> violated;  Cmd.Wait / os.Process.Wait   inconclusive -> violated;  Cmd.Start (control) unchanged\n  hs system / rawSystem / waitForProcess / getProcessExitCode   confirmed_with_caveats -> violated;  callProcess (control) unchanged\nPinned in tests/test_exit_status_is_one_verdict.py (red at the branch point: 40 failed; green after). smart-test (affected, 413 files): 12517 passed, 0 failed, changed files at 100% coverage.\n\nMEASURED COST (PLAN.md pre-registered before any arm; RESULT.md): 13 repos, both arms, 26/26 canaries. +103 situations, 0 removed, 13 widened, 5 verdicts inconclusive -> violated. Seeded sample 60/103: 0 carry the exit status to the sink (Wilson 95% upper 6.0%); 3 are real flows of subprocess.run's CAPTURED STDOUT (hence 21d86e2280); 57 are not flows; 0 useful. Pre-registered R2 fired: the false rows are the walk's declared blindnesses (not_attempted 73, escaped 12, structural 13 of 103; every DDG-confirmed row was real). Reported, not answered by removing rows. Bottom line: on this cohort the change buys consistency and zero useful findings; whether that cost stands is an owner call.\n\nFILED: WI-hifur-hulul-bikur-ridab-fozad-sagiv-dojuh-bogin (residual: c/cpp/JVM/scala/swift/objc/asyncio/os.spawn*/community typed-process), WI-hikuz-bafod-gomuk-piziz-podas-rihun-figad-forom (a Popen.wait -> later Popen flow is lost when the sink callee is also the receiver's constructor; undiagnosed recall gap)."  # 9ae2
