  clock: 4  # fbde
  nonce: fbde  # fbde
  message: "RE-MEASURE 2026-10-22, after the DDG stage (the owner's 2026-10-03 HOLD condition). Same pre-registered frame, cohort, claims, canaries, seed. BEFORE = dev 1f1e22d3f2; AFTER = jgstern-agent/fix/lanos rebased onto it (clean; 3 commits). Write-up: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/lanos_rerun_10212026/RESULT.md. RESULT: +614 situations by true evidence_count (2686 -> 3300; 10-03: +103), 0 true removals (R1 holds; the listed diff's 173 'removals' are rows pushed out of the 100-row evidence cap), the same 5 verdicts inconclusive -> violated (xmonad x2, fastapi x2, arti x1). Listed added rows by walk: not_attempted 84% (10-03: 71%), escaped 6%, ddg-confirmed 5%, structural 4%. Seeded sample 60: 0 carry the exit status to a sink (Wilson 95% upper 6.0%), 7 are captured-stdout flows (INV-lozat's run/stdout omission, caught incidentally), 53 not a flow (16 with the sink BEFORE the source), 0 useful. R2 fired again (false rows = the walk's not_attempted limit); R3 did not. BOTTOM LINE: the DDG stage did not shrink this family's noise -- it grew 6x and the walk attempts a smaller share. Owner decision needed: (a) keep holding, (b) the removal side (drop the os.wait*/Child.wait ipc_recv rows, INV-lozat's reading, ADR-0049 ruling 3), or (c) merge the omission side as measured. NOT VISIBLE to the sample: ~374 added situations beyond the evidence cap (qemu-meson, buildah); qemu-meson host-secret-no-logging +2 unexplained (beyond the cap)."  # fbde
- op: discuss  # 4184
  at: '2026-10-22T18:26:38Z'  # 4184
  by: agent  # 4184
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 4184
  clock: 5  # 4184
  nonce: '4184'  # 4184
  message: "OWNER DECISION 2026-10-22: option 2, the REMOVAL side, on two terms. (1) ADR-0049 is amended to say an exit status is not far-side \"content\" under Ruling 1, citing the 10-03 and 10-22 measurements: 0 of 120 sampled added findings carried an exit status to a sink, 0 useful, and the 5 verdicts that moved did not rest on an exit-status flow. (2) Ruling 3's finding-level test is run and passes BEFORE anything merges. The plan was pre-registered before any scan or arm: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/lanos_removal_10222026/PLAN.md. Any CORRECT removed situation, or a violated verdict that rested on one, is a STOP and goes back to the owner.\n\nReasoning given to the owner. Under ADR-0052 precision comes from which rows mint, not from the walk. The 10-03 hold condition (the DDG stage) has been met, and the noise grew (+103 -> +614), so holding has nothing left to wait for. The trust boundary for a hostile child is already its launch row, and the child's OUTPUT stays represented at check_output / communicate / Command.output / wait_with_output.\n\nPLAN. (a) Rows dropped: python os.wait / waitpid / wait3 / wait4 / waitid; rust Child.wait / try_wait. (b) ADR-0049 amendment, drafted for owner review. (c) From jgstern-agent/fix/lanos, keep the per-API reading of which calls return only a status, and turn test_exit_status_is_one_verdict into a test that pins AGREEMENT: the same verdict for the same value via os.waitpid and subprocess.call, Child.wait and Command::status. It pins agreement, not a pinned absence. The branch's omission-side rows are not merged. (d) The removal measurement runs after the stage-10 suites (heavy jobs one at a time).\n\nCONSEQUENCES FOR SIBLINGS. WI-hifur (extend minting to c/cpp/JVM/swift) is the omission side's residual and becomes moot -> wont_do once (b) lands. WI-hikuz's repro used Popen.wait as the source, which will not mint; its recall gap (a flow from a method on a Popen object to a later Popen call is lost) is re-stated against Popen.communicate, which does mint on dev. WI-rivur row 3 (os.wait) closes with this item.\n\nThe 7 captured-OUTPUT flows the sample found are a separate gap that none of the three options fixes. They are trackerized as two items (python subprocess.run stdout; go Cmd.Stdout buffer); ids are in the follow-up note."  # 4184
