  message: "RULING 3 MEASUREMENT DONE, OWNER APPROVED THE ADR-0049 AMENDMENT 2026-10-23. Pre-registered removal arms (lanos_removal_10222026/PLAN.md + AMENDMENTS 1-4): 11 repos (rust netavark arti livebook firecracker ripgrep; python grpc airflow pytorch qemu-u-boot mlflow envoy-half), BEFORE = dev 9b93a6396a, AFTER = same tree minus the os wait-family row and Child.wait/try_wait. Dropped: ceph (BEFORE hit the 3 h cap, AMENDMENT 2), virtualbox (8 h arm rule, AMENDMENT 3); envoy replaced by envoy-half (restarter/ + sha256-even files, both os.waitpid sites kept) after full envoy AFTER was SIGKILLed twice at ~20.5 GB (AMENDMENT 4; cause filed as INV-jahuf). Every canary passed. RESULT by TRUE evidence_count: removed 0, added 0, verdict moves 0, counts moved 0 (diff_all.txt). R1 census empty -> no STOP; R2 none; R3 holds; R4 holds (output primitives unchanged on fixtures). The comparison can fail: on fixtures the removal flips py-os-wait / py-os-waitpid / rs-child-wait from violated to no rows. Stated plainly: Ruling 3 holds because these rows produced no finding to lose on this corpus. Approved amendment text (v2): ADR-0049_amendment_DRAFT.md -- basis is INV-lozat's existing reading ('an exit status is not the child's message'), reason is the sink-argument/branch-condition point plus 0 of 120 sampled exit-status flows real, re-evaluation trigger stated, residual named. Residual filed: INV-sozak (wait_with_output().status / getstatusoutput()[0] / readProcessWithExitCode still mint; the agreement test pins that disagreement). NEXT: implement the row removal + agreement test from ~/hg_wt/lanos, amendment in the same PR."  # 1ffc
