  nonce: b39c  # b39c
  message: "DONE in PR #1825 (dev 397f2242e2): removal side, owner decision 2026-10-22, ADR-0049 amendment approved 2026-10-23. LIVE REPRO on merged dev, the item's own shape through the production CLI (verify-claims, claim untrusted-input-no-subprocess, cold XDG_CACHE_HOME per repo, --no-default-overlays): os.waitpid -> Popen: rc=3 confirmed_with_caveats, evidence 0; subprocess.call -> Popen: rc=3 confirmed_with_caveats, evidence 0; rust child.wait() (typed Child) -> Command::spawn: rc=3 confirmed_with_caveats, evidence 0; cmd.status() -> spawn: rc=3 confirmed_with_caveats, evidence 0. One value, one verdict. Control, the child's OUTPUT stays a source: subprocess.check_output -> Popen: rc=1 violated, evidence 1, source subprocess.check_output. At filing os.waitpid read violated and call confirmed_with_caveats. Ruling 3 measured before merge (lanos_removal_10222026/: 11 repos, 0 removed / 0 added / 0 verdict moves). Beyond the approved text, needed for the agreement to hold: a dated module_completeness entry for std::process::Child (enumerated from impl Child in std's process.rs) -- without it Child.wait was an unclassified call and read inconclusive vs Command::status's confirmed_with_caveats; the agreement test caught it, the corpus arms could not (WI-rupah). The exit-status family left CHOICE_SHAPED_SOURCE_NAMES. Residual pinned in the test as today's state: INV-sozak (wait_with_output().status / getstatusoutput()[0] still mint). Suite 23376 passed, gates 464."  # b39c
